# Untrusted folder: decline the trust dialog with Enter on the default
# cursor (0 == "No, exit" — internal/tui/dialog_trust.go's answer(cursor==1)
# is false here). "No, exit" means what it says: internal/tui/app.go's
# MsgTrustAnswered handler does `if !msg.Trusted { return m, tea.Quit }`, so
# declining quits the whole process rather than merely closing the dialog
# (corrected from an earlier version of this scenario that assumed the
# process stayed up — it does not, and never reaches "describe a task").
@faux testdata/faux/hello.yaml
@size 120x40
@untrusted

WAITFOR /Accessing workspace/ 20
SHOT trust-dialog-decline
EXPECT /No, exit/
KEY enter
WAIT 1
SHOT trust-declined
NOTE kiln should have exited on decline; nothing further to type
EXPECT_NOT /panic|goroutine/
